---
description: Brain plugin tools are plural — accept and return sets, never make the agent loop over single calls
globs: brain/plugins/**,brain/websearch/**,test/brain/plugins/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Plugin tools are plural

A tool call costs tokens, a round trip, and a model turn. No tool may force
the agent into N calls for N items. Every tool thinks in sets.

- **Input accepts a set.** Dates take a range (`start`/`end`, or `days`) or a
  list; ids/names take a list; lookups take a prefix or pattern. The single
  form stays accepted for compatibility, and no argument means "today" /
  "the obvious default", never an error.
- **Output is a list.** Even one match comes back as `[item]`. Per-item
  failures are rows inside the list (`{ date, error }`), not a failed call.
- **Keep the Go name and the Go fields.** Extend `inputSchema` additively
  (`date` stays; add `start`, `end`, `dates`). Prompts and eval fixtures key on
  the names.
- **Inherently singular tools** (`account_get`, `utility_get_current_date`,
  `*_create` of one record) set `single: "<why>"` on the `ToolDef`. The
  test `test/brain/plugins/plural.test.ts` fails any tool that is neither
  plural nor annotated.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — seven calls for a week
sleep_get({ date: "2026-10-05" })

// ✅ GOOD — one call, one list
sleep_get({ start: "2026-10-05", end: "2026-10-11" })
// → [{ date: "2026-10-05", ... }, ..., { date: "2026-10-11", ... }]

// ❌ BAD — exact title only
docs_search({ title: "tesla notes" })

// ✅ GOOD — prefix / pattern, all matches
drive_search_files({ name_prefix: "tes" })
// → [{ id, name: "tesla notes" }, { id, name: "test plan" }]
```

Cap list sizes the way the Go server capped pages (`limit`, default sane,
max documented in the description) so one call cannot blow the context.
